## Effect-System End-to-End Integration — B.8 acceptance spec.
##
## Operation Piezoelectric Effects, Phase 1, Milestone B (chunk B.8).
## Final integration test for the type-system layer of the effect epic.
## Exercises every B chunk in concert:
##
##   B.1: registry storage admits the row + effect-decl tables.
##   B.2: `effect Name end` registers via NODE_EFFECT_DECL pre-pass.
##   B.3: `def fn() ... can Row` attaches the parsed row onto fn's AST.
##   B.4: tc_row_unify (here exercised indirectly via B.7's call-site).
##   B.5: tc_row_substitute / occurs-check (no-op so far — B.6+ wiring).
##   B.6: tc_row_subsume primitive.
##   B.7: tc_expr_call invokes subsume → emits QZ0610 on mismatch.
##
## What B does NOT yet do (deferred to Milestone C / B.7-followup):
## - Effect-op call automatically widens the caller's row.
## - `with H do -> body end` narrows the body's row by H's handled
##   effects. (Parser still discards the handler expression — see
##   parser.qz:4787 — so typecheck has nothing to inspect.)
##
## So the demo program below uses an UNTRACKED top-level main() to
## sidestep the missing handler-narrowing. main has no `can` clause,
## so it short-circuits the row check at every call site, allowing it
## to invoke `parse` (which does have `can Throws`) without an
## intermediate handler. The check ONLY fires when both caller and
## callee have non-untracked rows — exactly Milestone B's deliverable.

import * from qspec
import * from qspec/subprocess

def main(): Int
  describe("Milestone B end-to-end: effect declarations + can rows + QZ0610") do ->
    it("declare effect, declare can-rowed function, call from untracked main — compiles") do ->
      assert_compile_succeeds("""
effect Throws
  def throw(msg: String): Int
end

def parse(s: String): Int can Throws = 42

def main(): Int = parse("42")
""")
    end

    it("two compatible can-rowed functions in chain — compiles") do ->
      assert_compile_succeeds("""
effect Log
end

def emit(): Int can Log = 1
def relay(): Int can Log = emit()
def main(): Int = relay()
""")
    end

    it("can-rowed callee from narrower can-rowed caller — QZ0610") do ->
      assert_compile_error("""
effect Log
end

effect Trace
end

def deep(): Int can Log, Trace = 1
def shallow(): Int can Log = deep()
def main(): Int = shallow()
""", "QZ0610")
    end

    it("effect declaration + bare-can fn that calls Throws-rowed callee — QZ0610") do ->
      assert_compile_error("""
effect Throws
  def throw(s: String): Int
end

def fail(): Int can Throws = 0
def pure_ish(): Int can = fail()
def main(): Int = pure_ish()
""", "QZ0610")
    end

    it("open-tail caller absorbs callee's extra effects — compiles") do ->
      assert_compile_succeeds("""
effect Log
end

effect Trace
end

def both(): Int can Log, Trace = 1
def open_caller(): Int can Log | r = both()
def main(): Int = open_caller()
""")
    end
  end
  return qspec_main()
end
